# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@thread brace_quest
# en: The captain's charm
name [7a7935] = 队长的护符
# en: An old captain's charm in the duelling dummy empties only if someone holds firm while it fires.
premise [ac57f9] = 决斗木人里有一枚老队长的护符，只有在它开火时有人站稳不退，才能把它耗空。
# en: You said you'd try to empty the old captain's charm. Someone drew a stretcher under your name.
journal.1 [1f5a84] = 你说你要试着耗空那枚老队长的护符。有人在你名字下面画了副担架。
# en: The captain's notes: don't stop the first blow, let it land on something that isn't you.
journal.2 [4d5179] = 队长的笔记：别去挡第一击，让它落在不是你的东西上。
# en: Bram threw hexes at you in the chalk circle until he ran out.
journal.3 [e55913] = 布拉姆在粉笔圈里朝你扔咒，一直扔到他没了力气。
# en: Lyra drilled your stance until dark. "Better," she said.
journal.4 [60ee21] = 莱拉逼你练站姿直到天黑。“好些了，”她说。
# en: The first time, the charm lifted you clean out of the circle.
journal.5 [c76d4f] = 第一次，那枚护符把你整个掀出了圈子。
# en: You held the circle until the charm sputtered out. Lyra nodded, once.
journal.6 [a44c67] = 你守住了圈子，直到护符噗地熄灭。莱拉点了一下头。

@event duel_dummy_hexes
# en: The Dummy Hits Back
title [73ba1d] = 假人反击了
# en: The eyepatched dummy has started throwing hexes back. Lyra splits its seam and pulls out an old captain's charm, sewn in decades ago and still humming. "It empties if someone holds firm in the circle while it fires," she says. "Nobody's managed it. Nobody's tried properly."
text [81980f] = 那个戴眼罩的假人开始把恶咒扔回来了。莱拉拆开它的接缝，拽出一枚老队长的护符，是几十年前缝进去的，至今还在嗡嗡作响。“只要有人在圈里站稳、等它放完，它就空了，”她说，“没人做到过。没人好好试过。”
# en: A duel hall's practice corner, an eyepatched straw dummy flinging a crackling hex back at a startled student, stuffing spilling from a split seam.
scene [23661b] = 决斗厅的练习角落，一个戴眼罩的草人朝一个吓了一跳的学生甩回一道噼啪作响的恶咒，裂开的接缝里漏出稻草。
# en: "I'll try properly."
opt.left.label [91bd61] = “我来好好试试。”
# en: Lyra sews the charm back in, looks at you, and writes your name on the board under the dummy. Underneath, someone adds a small drawing of a stretcher.
opt.left.say.1 [61b029] = 莱拉把护符缝了回去，看了看你，把你的名字写在假人下方的板子上。下面有人添了一个小小的担架图。
# en: Leave it to the seniors
opt.right.label [08b604] = 留给高年级生
# en: You go back to your bout, and the dummy goes back to hexing whoever passes. A senior limps past at the end of practice, still smoking slightly.
opt.right.say.1 [3e1dce] = 你回去打你的那一局，假人回去对每个路过的人放恶咒。练习结束时，一个高年级生一瘸一拐地走过，身上还冒着点烟。

@event duel_captains_notes
# en: The Captain's Notes
title [ca8e13] = 队长的笔记
# en: The captain who made the charm left notes, in a cupboard under the trophy shelf, in a hand like barbed wire. Half of it is about footwork and the other half is insults addressed to people long graduated.
text [718aeb] = 造护符的那位队长留下了笔记，就在奖杯架下的柜子里，字迹像带刺的铁丝。一半讲步法，另一半是写给早已毕业之人的骂话。
# en: A dusty cupboard in the duel hall, a student reading a cracked leather notebook by the light of a single lamp.
scene [a225a8] = 决斗厅里一个落满灰的柜子，一个学生借着一盏孤灯读一本开裂的皮面笔记本。
# en: Read them properly
opt.left.label [58ece6] = 好好读一遍
# en: Between the insults is the trick: you don't stop the first blow, you let it land on something that isn't you. You copy the page out and put the notebook back where the captain would have wanted it.
opt.left.say.1 [a2ca36] = 在骂话之间藏着诀窍：你不去挡第一击，而是让它落在不是你的东西上。你把那一页抄下来，把笔记本放回队长会希望的位置。
# en: You read until the lamp gutters and learn a great deal about a student called Pim, who could not parry. The trick is in there somewhere. You'll have to come back for it.
opt.left.say.2 [c40f86] = 你读到灯芯快灭，对一个叫皮姆、怎么也学不会格挡的学生了解了很多。诀窍就在里面某处。你只能改天再来。
# en: Spar instead tonight
opt.right.label [ced9ea] = 今晚改去对练
# en: You leave the notes for another evening and take a bout instead. You win it, which is the other kind of useful.
opt.right.say.1 [cbb7a5] = 你把笔记留到另一个晚上，去打了一局。你赢了，这是另一种有用。

@event duel_bram_barrage
# en: Inside the Chalk Circle
title [6ebe8b] = 粉笔圈里
# en: Word reaches Bram that you mean to empty the captain's charm. He turns up with his sleeves rolled. "Regulation hazing," he announces, "section four. You stand in the circle. I throw. You don't step out. Ready?"
text [ebedae] = 布拉姆听说你打算放空队长的护符。他挽着袖子来了。“标准欺新，”他宣布，“第四条。你站在圈里。我扔。你不许出圈。准备好了吗？”
# en: A student standing in a chalk circle on a scorched floor while a broad prefect hurls a stream of stinging hexes from the edge.
scene [0fd424] = 一个学生站在烧焦地板上的粉笔圈里，一个魁梧的级长从圈边连珠炮似的扔出蛰人的恶咒。
# en: Hold the circle against him
opt.left.label [d2886c] = 在圈里顶住他
# en: You don't step out. By the twentieth hex Bram is red in the face and you are still in the circle, scorched and planted. "Adequate," he says, gruffly, and doesn't put you on report.
opt.left.say.1 [2ebcf5] = 你没出圈。到第二十道恶咒时，布拉姆满脸通红，你还站在圈里，焦了，却扎了根。“尚可，”他粗声说，没有记你的过。
# en: The ninth hex knocks you clean out of the circle. Bram notes it in his book. "Section four, failed," he says. "Again next week."
opt.left.say.2 [dc3867] = 第九道恶咒把你掀出了圈。布拉姆在本子上记下。“第四条，未通过，”他说，“下周再来。”
# en: Take it all on your shield arm
opt.right.label [e34207] = 全用盾牌手臂扛
# en: You don't try to be clever. You just stand there and take it, every hex, on your arm, until Bram runs out. Your arm is purple for a week. Bram looks almost impressed.
opt.right.say.1 [33cb6d] = 你没耍聪明。你就站在那儿扛，每一道恶咒都落在胳膊上，直到布拉姆扔完。你的胳膊紫了一周。布拉姆看上去几乎有点佩服。
# en: Shrug it off in the coat
opt.up.label [46b38b] = 穿着外套硬扛
# en: You button the quilted coat to the chin and plant your feet. The hexes thud into the padding like snowballs into a wall. Bram runs out first. "That's cheating," he says. "Section four doesn't mention coats," you say.
opt.up.say.1 [eeb3c5] = 你把绗缝外套扣到下巴，站稳脚跟。恶咒砸进衬垫，像雪球砸在墙上。布拉姆先扔完了。“这算作弊，”他说。“第四条可没提外套，”你说。

@event duel_footwork_lyra
# en: Footwork Until Dark
title [b94ac8] = 练步法到天黑
# en: Lyra finds you after practice. "The captain's notes say the stance is everything," she says. "Your stance is a disgrace. Three hours. Now." She has already chalked the marks on the floor.
text [2d594e] = 练习后莱拉找到你。“队长笔记说站姿就是一切，”她说，“你的站姿是个耻辱。三个钟头。现在。”她已经在地上画好了粉笔记号。
# en: An empty duel hall at dusk, two students drilling footwork across chalk marks, one of them pointing sharply at the other's feet.
scene [95915c] = 黄昏空荡荡的决斗厅，两个学生沿着粉笔记号练步法，其中一人严厉地指着另一人的脚。
# en: Drill until dark
opt.left.label [811d2a] = 练到天黑
# en: She is merciless and exact. By dark you can set your feet without thinking, and you never want to see a chalk mark again. "Better," she says, which from Lyra is a sonnet.
opt.left.say.1 [237639] = 她毫不留情，分毫不差。到天黑，你不假思索就能站稳脚步，而且这辈子都不想再看见粉笔记号。“好些了，”她说，从莱拉嘴里出来这就是一首十四行诗。
# en: "Tomorrow. I have an essay."
opt.right.label [3c02a9] = “明天吧。我有篇论文。”
# en: She looks at you as if you'd chosen to lose. You write the essay. It is a fine essay, and Lyra mentions your stance at breakfast.
opt.right.say.1 [fd14f0] = 她看着你，好像你是自己选择了认输。你写了论文。那是篇不错的论文，早饭时莱拉提起了你的站姿。

@event duel_brace_final
# en: Hold Firm
title [7cdab4] = 站稳
# en: The club gathers on the benches. You step into the chalk circle, and the eyepatched dummy turns its head toward you with an audible creak. The captain's charm begins to fire. {flag(brace_notes) and flag(brace_circle) and flag(brace_footwork): You know how to stand, and why.|You have done some of the work. Not all of it.}
text [251e18] = 社员们聚到长凳上。你走进粉笔圈，那个戴眼罩的假人嘎吱一声朝你转过头来。队长的护符开始发射。{flag(brace_notes) and flag(brace_circle) and flag(brace_footwork): 你知道该怎么站，也知道为什么。|你做了一部分功课。不是全部。}
# en: A student standing firm in a chalk circle in a crowded duel hall as an eyepatched dummy fires hex after hex, the club watching from the benches.
scene [d18fe2] = 一个学生在挤满人的决斗厅里稳稳站在粉笔圈中，一个戴眼罩的假人一道接一道地放恶咒，社员们在长凳上看着。
# en: Hold firm
opt.left.label [5c71d4] = 站稳
# en: The hexes break on you one after another, and each lands softer than the last. When the charm finally sputters out, the club is on its feet. Lyra doesn't clap. She nods, once, which is louder.
opt.left.say.1 [2151b8] = 恶咒一道接一道在你身上碎开，每一道都比上一道轻。护符终于噼啪一声熄了，全社都站了起来。莱拉没有鼓掌。她点了一下头，这比掌声更响。
# en: The fourteenth hex lifts you out of the circle and into the benches. The dummy turns its head back with a creak. It will be there at practice, waiting.
opt.left.say.2 [98d202] = 第十四道恶咒把你从圈里掀到了长凳上。假人嘎吱一声把头转了回去。它会在练习时等着你。
# en: Borrow the captain's old gauntlets
opt.right.label [eaf6bb] = 借老队长的护手
# en: The club quartermaster rents you the captain's own gauntlets for the night. They take the first blow for you, and the rest you take yourself. When the charm sputters out, the benches roar.
opt.right.say.1 [0c809b] = 社里的管理员把老队长自己的护手借给你一晚上。它们替你挡下了第一击，剩下的你自己扛。护符噼啪熄灭时，长凳上一片欢呼。
# en: Even in the gauntlets, the fourteenth hex lifts you out of the circle. The rental is not refunded. The dummy creaks its head back and waits.
opt.right.say.2 [586ef6] = 就算戴着护手，第十四道恶咒还是把你掀出了圈。租金不退。假人嘎吱一声转回头，等着。

@thread quickquill_quest
# en: The quill that talks back
name [0707e8] = 会顶嘴的羽毛笔
# en: A spare quill at the Ledger has started inventing your sentences.
premise [9309d1] = 《纪事报》的一支备用羽毛笔，开始替你编句子了。
# en: You took the Ledger's runaway quill home in a handkerchief. It wrote "kidnapped" on it.
journal.1 [7175c8] = 你用手帕把《纪事报》那支不听话的羽毛笔裹回了家。它在手帕上写了“绑架”。
# en: You kept the quill to the facts on forty letters about the soup.
journal.2 [eac39c] = 四十封关于汤的投诉信，你都按住了羽毛笔，只写事实。
# en: You bought it proper ink, black as a well. It underlines the bits you'll need.
journal.3 [8cdeed] = 你给它买了上好的墨水，黑得像口井。它会把你用得着的地方划出来。
# en: You and the quill wrote until four on deadline night. Nessa put your name on the page.
journal.4 [0291f7] = 截稿那夜，你和羽毛笔一直写到四点。内莎把你的名字印上了版面。
# en: The first interview got away from you, and from the quill.
journal.5 [8c283b] = 第一次采访，你和羽毛笔都没能把住。
# en: The chair denied everything, word for word. "Front page," said Nessa.
journal.6 [b747a9] = 委员会主席什么都否认，一字不差地被记了下来。“头版，”内莎说。

@event ledger_spare_quill
# en: The Spare Quill
title [29f326] = 备用羽毛笔
# en: A spare quill on the drying line has been finishing your sentences. Today it started inventing them: your proof now says the refectory serves dragon. "Oh, it's woken up," says Nessa, delighted. "Tame it and it's yours. Nobody's tamed one since I've been editor."
text [b0d093] = 晾稿绳上的一支备用羽毛笔一直在替你把话写完。今天它开始自己编了：你的校样上现在写着膳堂供应龙肉。“哦，它醒了，”内莎高兴地说，“驯服它，它就归你。我当编辑以来还没人驯服过一支。”
# en: A newspaper office with proofs pegged on a drying line, a lone quill hanging among them scribbling on a proof by itself.
scene [a7cf40] = 一间报社，校样夹在晾稿绳上，一支孤零零的羽毛笔挂在其中，自己在一张校样上涂写。
# en: Take the quill home
opt.left.label [53212f] = 把羽毛笔带回家
# en: You wrap it in a handkerchief. It writes "kidnapped" on the handkerchief. Nessa writes your name on the office board under QUILL, with a question mark.
opt.left.say.1 [c856e1] = 你用手帕把它包起来。它在手帕上写了“绑架”。内莎在办公室的板子上“羽毛笔”下面写了你的名字，后面打了个问号。
# en: Peg it back on the line
opt.right.label [db33eb] = 把它夹回绳上
# en: You peg it back. It writes a small, hurt editorial about you on the next proof, which Nessa cuts, laughing.
opt.right.say.1 [c59c09] = 你把它夹了回去。它在下一张校样上写了一篇受伤的小社论讲你，内莎笑着把它删了。

@event ledger_soup_complaint
# en: The Soup Complaint
title [d5021e] = 汤的投诉
# en: Forty furious letters about the refectory soup have arrived. Nessa wants one calm reply, printed. You decide to dictate it to the quill, which wants very badly to make it more exciting.
text [7caf2e] = 关于膳堂的汤，来了四十封怒气冲冲的信。内莎要一篇冷静的回复，要登出来。你决定口述给那支羽毛笔，而它非常想把回复写得更刺激些。
# en: A desk buried in angry letters about soup, a student dictating firmly to a quill that keeps trying to add flourishes.
scene [9b8d46] = 一张被关于汤的愤怒来信淹没的书桌，一个学生坚定地对一支总想加点花样的羽毛笔口述。
# en: Keep the quill to the facts
opt.left.label [38c15f] = 让羽毛笔只写事实
# en: Every time it reaches for a flourish, you catch it. The reply comes out calm, true and very dull. Nessa prints it. The quill sulks, and then, grudgingly, writes the next one straight.
opt.left.say.1 [1545a6] = 它每次伸手去加花样，你都把它截住。回复写得冷静、真实，而且非常无聊。内莎登了。羽毛笔闹了脾气，然后不情不愿地把下一封写得规规矩矩。
# en: You blink and the quill has written that the soup contains a mild curse. It prints. You spend Thursday apologising to the cooks.
opt.left.say.2 [f1776c] = 一眨眼，羽毛笔写了汤里有轻微诅咒。登出来了。你花了整个周四向厨子们道歉。
# en: Write the reply by hand
opt.right.label [54b39d] = 亲手写回复
# en: You write it yourself, slowly. It's a good reply. The quill watches from the inkwell, offended at being left out.
opt.right.say.1 [4ad58a] = 你自己写，写得很慢。回复不错。羽毛笔从墨水瓶里看着，因为被晾在一边而生气。

@event ledger_proper_ink
# en: Proper Ink
title [c79087] = 像样的墨水
# en: The quill refuses the school ink. It blots, it sulks, it writes "no" in large letters. The stationer in the village has proper ink, black as a well and priced like it.
text [7d5688] = 羽毛笔拒绝学校的墨水。它洇墨、闹脾气、用大字写“不”。村里的文具店有像样的墨水，黑得像井，价钱也一样深。
# en: A stationer's counter in the village, a student holding a small dark bottle of ink up to the light while a quill pokes out of their pocket.
scene [fd2560] = 村里文具店的柜台，一个学生举起一小瓶深色墨水对着光看，口袋里探出一支羽毛笔。
# en: Buy the proper ink
opt.left.label [98fa9e] = 买像样的墨水
# en: The quill drinks the new ink and writes a whole page of your notes, neatly, in a better hand than yours. It underlines the bits you'll need. You feel slightly managed.
opt.left.say.1 [b2fa8a] = 羽毛笔喝下新墨水，替你整整齐齐写了一整页笔记，字比你的还好看。它还把你要用的地方划了线。你觉得自己有点被安排了。
# en: Make it use the school ink
opt.right.label [0f3f50] = 让它用学校的墨水
# en: It uses the school ink under protest and blots every third word, including, pointedly, your name.
opt.right.say.1 [c3e17e] = 它不情不愿地用着学校的墨水，每三个字洇一个，包括——显然是故意的——你的名字。

@event ledger_deadline_night
# en: Deadline Night
title [d06cb7] = 截稿夜
# en: Deadline night. The front page fell through at nine and Nessa is pacing. "We need eight hundred words by four," she says. "Anybody with a quill that writes fast, now is the time."
text [a82a66] = 截稿夜。九点头版泡了汤，内莎来回踱步。“四点前我们需要八百字，”她说，“谁有写得快的羽毛笔，现在就是时候。”
# en: A newspaper office after midnight, cold tea and candle stubs everywhere, a student and a quill working side by side while an editor paces.
scene [3fdd7a] = 午夜后的报社，到处是冷茶和蜡烛头，一个学生和一支羽毛笔并肩工作，一位编辑来回踱步。
# en: Sit it out with the quill
opt.left.label [921566] = 陪羽毛笔熬过去
# en: You and the quill write until four. By the end it finishes your sentences only when you want it to. You are both too tired to argue. Nessa puts your name on the page, small.
opt.left.say.1 [dd5438] = 你和羽毛笔一直写到四点。到最后，只有你想让它接话时它才接。你们俩都累得吵不动了。内莎把你的名字印在版面上，字很小。
# en: Go to bed
opt.right.label [2fa817] = 去睡觉
# en: You sleep. In the morning the front page is late and Nessa is hoarse, and the quill has written a bitter little poem about you on the pillowcase.
opt.right.say.1 [c3ec9a] = 你睡了。早上头版晚了，内莎嗓子哑了，羽毛笔在你的枕套上写了一首关于你的刻薄小诗。

@event ledger_quill_interview
# en: Deny Everything
title [745920] = 一概否认
# en: Nessa sends you to interview the chair of the refectory committee, who will deny everything, including the soup. "Get it word for word," she says. "Every word. They'll deny the words too." {flag(quickquill_soup) and flag(quickquill_ink) and flag(quickquill_deadline): Your quill sits up in your pocket, ready.|Your quill is half-tamed at best.}
text [df81a3] = 内莎派你去采访膳堂委员会主席，那人会一概否认，包括那锅汤。“一字不落地记下来，”她说，“每一个字。他们连说过的字都会否认。”{flag(quickquill_soup) and flag(quickquill_ink) and flag(quickquill_deadline): 你的羽毛笔在口袋里坐直了，随时待命。|你的羽毛笔充其量驯服了一半。}
# en: A stuffy committee room, a smooth official smiling across a table at a student whose quill writes furiously on its own.
scene [a90711] = 一间闷热的委员会会议室，一位圆滑的官员隔着桌子朝一个学生微笑，学生的羽毛笔正自己飞快地写着。
# en: Interview them with the quill
opt.left.label [b85ec0] = 带着羽毛笔去采访
# en: The chair denies everything, and the quill takes every denial down word for word, including the one that contradicts the other three. Nessa reads it and goes very quiet. "Front page," she says.
opt.left.say.1 [432baf] = 主席一概否认，羽毛笔把每一句否认都逐字记下，包括与另外三句自相矛盾的那一句。内莎读完，安静了下来。“头版，”她说。
# en: The quill gets bored halfway and starts improving the chair's answers. Nothing is printable. The quill sulks in the WILL NOT PRINT basket until your next front page.
opt.left.say.2 [46c476] = 羽毛笔到一半就腻了，开始替主席润色回答。一个字都不能登。羽毛笔在“不予刊登”的篮子里赌气，直到你下一次上头版。
# en: Prepare all night first
opt.right.label [fa7c4f] = 先通宵准备
# en: You go in tired and over-prepared, with every question written out. The quill follows your lead all the way through. Nessa reads the transcript twice. "Front page."
opt.right.say.1 [6bc6d3] = 你带着倦意、准备过头地去了，每个问题都写好了。羽毛笔从头到尾都跟着你的节奏。内莎把记录读了两遍。“头版。”
# en: All night's preparation, and the chair simply doesn't turn up. The quill sulks in the WILL NOT PRINT basket until your next front page.
opt.right.say.2 [d13a9a] = 准备了一整夜，主席干脆没来。羽毛笔在“不予刊登”的篮子里赌气，直到你下一次上头版。

@thread bramble_quest
# en: The seed in your pocket
name [e1a78b] = 口袋里的种子
# en: A hedge-seed that chose you, and has already put out a shoot.
premise [53a28f] = 一颗挑中了你的篱笆种，已经冒出了芽。
# en: "That's a hedge-seed," Tobias said. "They choose people." This one chose you.
journal.1 [aed022] = “这是篱笆种，”托比亚斯说，“它们会自己挑人。”这一颗挑中了你。
# en: You found your seedling a bed of its own.
journal.2 [5b1e6f] = 你给你的幼苗找了一块属于它的苗床。
# en: You sat up with it through the first frost, feeding it warmth. It grew a thorn.
journal.3 [f21750] = 第一场霜降那夜，你守着它，喂它温暖。它长出了一根刺。
# en: You quieted the mandrake choir, and your seedling put out a vine.
journal.4 [449e35] = 你让曼德拉草合唱团安静了下来，你的幼苗抽出了一根藤。
# en: The night it bolted, the hedge didn't know you yet.
journal.5 [5d180b] = 它疯长的那一夜，那片荆篱还不认得你。
# en: The night it bolted across the greenhouse, it stopped for you.
journal.6 [1108fa] = 它在温室里疯长的那一夜，为你停了下来。

@event verdant_far_bed
# en: The Far Bed Answers
title [d21f95] = 最里头的苗床回话了
# en: The far bed answers back today: every vine in it turns to follow you. On the way out you find a seed in your coat pocket that wasn't there this morning, and it has already put out a shoot.
text [f601cf] = 今天最里头那块苗床回话了：苗床里每一根藤都转过来跟着你。出门时，你在外套口袋里发现一颗早上还没有的种子，它已经冒出了一根芽。
# en: The far end of a greenhouse, a tangle of vines reaching toward a student who has just found a green shoot curling out of their coat pocket.
scene [00541a] = 温室的尽头，一团藤蔓朝一个学生伸过来，学生刚发现外套口袋里卷出一根绿芽。
# en: Keep it and grow it
opt.left.label [49383c] = 留着它，养大它
# en: You cup it in your palm. The shoot curls round your finger, firmly. Tobias, when you show him, goes pale and then delighted. "That's a hedge-seed," he says. "They choose people."
opt.left.say.1 [0bab8b] = 你把它捧在掌心。那根芽稳稳地缠住了你的手指。你拿给托比亚斯看时，他先是脸色发白，然后高兴起来。“这是篱笆种，”他说，“它们会自己挑人。”
# en: Give it to Tobias
opt.right.label [e597fe] = 交给托比亚斯
# en: Tobias takes it gently and puts it in a pot by the door. "It'll want you back," he says. "They usually do."
opt.right.say.1 [ce4a73] = 托比亚斯轻轻接过，把它种进门边的花盆。“它会想你的，”他说，“它们通常都会。”

@event verdant_plant_seed
# en: Somewhere to Grow
title [ca8d3c] = 找个地方生长
# en: The seed has outgrown your pocket. It needs a bed. Tobias offers the corner of his own in the greenhouse. Old Maud, passing, says there's a corner in her garden that never gets frost, "if you can keep a secret, dearie."
text [0d1c6a] = 那颗种子已经装不下你的口袋了。它需要一块苗床。托比亚斯把自己那块的一角让给你。老莫德路过时说，她的花园里有个角落从不结霜，“要是你守得住秘密的话，亲爱的。”
# en: Two students kneeling in a greenhouse bed planting a seedling, a lantern between them and earth up to their elbows.
scene [d4bbf7] = 两个学生跪在温室苗床里种一株幼苗，中间放着一盏灯，泥土一直沾到手肘。
# en: Plant it with Tobias
opt.left.label [57094f] = 和托比亚斯一起种
# en: You plant it together by lantern light, and Tobias tells it a long story about a goat to help it settle. It settles. So does Tobias, eventually.
opt.left.say.1 [2baafd] = 你们在灯下一起把它种下，托比亚斯给它讲了一个关于山羊的长故事，帮它安下心来。它安下心来了。托比亚斯过了一会儿也是。
# en: Plant it in Maud's garden
opt.right.label [401918] = 种在莫德的花园里
# en: Maud leads you through a door you'd never noticed into a garden you'll never find on your own. You plant it there. "It'll be happy," she says, "for a while."
opt.right.say.1 [5eda0e] = 莫德领你穿过一扇你从没注意过的门，进了一个你自己永远找不到的花园。你把它种在那儿。“它会开心的，”她说，“开心一阵子。”

@event verdant_cold_snap
# en: The Cold Snap
title [deb4a6] = 寒潮
# en: A hard frost is coming tonight, the first of the season. Your seedling is too young for it. Somebody would have to sit with it till dawn, feeding it warmth.
text [b3caad] = 今晚要下一场重霜，是这一季的头一场。你的幼苗还太小，扛不住。得有人陪它坐到天亮，把暖意喂给它。
# en: Frost creeping over a greenhouse bed at night, a student wrapped in a blanket sitting beside a shivering seedling with a lantern.
scene [888a42] = 夜里白霜爬上温室苗床，一个裹着毯子的学生提着灯坐在一株瑟瑟发抖的幼苗旁。
# en: Sit up with it all night
opt.left.label [18ab48] = 陪它坐一整夜
# en: You sit wrapped round the lantern till dawn, feeding it what warmth you have. By morning you're stiff and coughing, and the seedling has grown a thorn, which it seems proud of.
opt.left.say.1 [912299] = 你裹着灯一直坐到天亮，把自己能给的暖意都喂给它。到早上你浑身僵硬、咳个不停，幼苗长出了一根刺，看上去很是得意。
# en: Cover it and hope
opt.right.label [36916e] = 盖上，听天由命
# en: You cover it with sacking and go to bed. It survives, sulking, and loses a leaf. It is noticeably cooler towards you.
opt.right.say.1 [0ad654] = 你用麻袋把它盖上就去睡了。它活下来了，赌着气，掉了一片叶子。它对你明显冷淡了。

@event verdant_mandrake_choir
# en: The Mandrake Choir
title [a16982] = 曼德拉草合唱团
# en: The mandrakes in the next bed have taken against your seedling and scream at it in chorus every evening. It's wilting from the noise. Gerald is conducting.
text [db08b7] = 隔壁苗床的曼德拉草看你的幼苗不顺眼，每天傍晚齐声冲它尖叫。它被吵得蔫了。杰拉尔德在指挥。
# en: A row of potted mandrakes in knitted hats screaming in chorus at a nervous seedling, a student with earmuffs approaching with a watering can.
scene [500265] = 一排戴着针织帽的盆栽曼德拉草齐声冲一株紧张的幼苗尖叫，一个戴着耳罩的学生提着水壶走近。
# en: Quiet the choir
opt.left.label [0b5253] = 让合唱团安静
# en: A drop of valerian in each pot and a firm word with Gerald, and the choir settles into a low hum. Your seedling straightens up and puts out a vine.
opt.left.say.1 [163e3b] = 每盆滴一滴缬草，再跟杰拉尔德严肃地谈一谈，合唱团就降成了低低的哼唱。你的幼苗直起腰，伸出了一根藤。
# en: The choir screams at you instead. Your ears ring till supper. Gerald looks unrepentant in his hat.
opt.left.say.2 [4a8e2e] = 合唱团转而冲你尖叫。你的耳朵一直嗡嗡响到晚饭。杰拉尔德戴着帽子，毫无悔意。
# en: Move the seedling's pot
opt.right.label [619d89] = 把幼苗的盆挪开
# en: You move it to the quiet end. It perks up, but it's away from the warm pipes now, and it isn't growing.
opt.right.say.1 [f49f23] = 你把它挪到安静的那头。它精神了，但现在离暖管远了，长不动了。

@event verdant_bramble_bolts
# en: The Night It Bolts
title [256113] = 疯长之夜
# en: Tobias wakes you at midnight. Your plant has bolted: a hedge of thorns is surging across the greenhouse toward the moonflower beds, and it is not stopping for anyone but you. {flag(bramble_fed) and flag(bramble_choir): It knows your voice.|You're not sure it knows you at all.}
text [0b7d5b] = 午夜托比亚斯把你叫醒。你的植物疯长了：一道荆棘树篱正横扫温室，冲向月光花的苗床，除了你谁也拦不住。{flag(bramble_fed) and flag(bramble_choir): 它认得你的声音。|你不确定它到底认不认得你。}
# en: A greenhouse at night, a thorny hedge surging across the beds toward a row of pale flowers, a student with arms outstretched trying to hold it back.
scene [26a79e] = 夜里的温室，一道带刺的树篱横扫苗床，冲向一排苍白的花，一个学生张开双臂想拦住它。
# en: Call it to heel
opt.left.label [ea558f] = 唤它回来
# en: You put out your hand and the hedge stops a finger's width from the moonflowers, then folds itself back into your palm like a sleeping cat. Tobias sits down on a bucket and laughs from the belly.
opt.left.say.1 [ee8753] = 你伸出手，树篱在离月光花一指宽的地方停下，然后像一只睡着的猫一样卷回你的掌心。托比亚斯一屁股坐在水桶上，从肚子里笑了出来。
# en: The thorns take your sleeve and some of your arm before Tobias shears it back. Maud keeps a cutting, and says she'll offer it to you again in Stormbloom.
opt.left.say.2 [d878fc] = 荆棘扯走了你的袖子和你胳膊上的一些皮，托比亚斯才把它剪了回去。莫德留了一截插枝，说风暴月时会再给你一次机会。
# en: Wade in and grab the root
opt.right.label [ac8d4f] = 蹚进去抓住根
# en: You wade through thorns to the root and hold it. The hedge goes still, then curls round you instead, gently. You're scratched to ribbons and it's yours.
opt.right.say.1 [f23f29] = 你蹚过荆棘找到根，把它握住。树篱静了下来，然后转而轻轻地缠住你。你被划得遍体鳞伤，但它是你的了。
# en: You get the root and it gets you. Tobias shears the hedge back by dawn. Maud keeps a cutting for Stormbloom.
opt.right.say.2 [01dde4] = 你抓住了根，它也抓住了你。天亮前托比亚斯把树篱剪了回去。莫德为风暴月留了一截插枝。

@thread index_quest
# en: Footnote's drawer
name [f8bf3c] = 脚注的抽屉
# en: The library cat guards a card for a book eleven years overdue.
premise [7b0eb8] = 图书馆的猫守着一张卡片，卡上那本书已经逾期十一年。
# en: Footnote was guarding the card of a book on wards, borrowed by Professor Thorne eleven years ago.
journal.1 [58af1d] = 脚注守着的是一本结界书的借书卡，十一年前由索恩教授借走。
# en: A proper herring bought you the card, and apparently the cat.
journal.2 [1f0570] = 一条像样的鲱鱼换来了那张卡片，看样子还换来了那只猫。
# en: You walked the night hush with the old lamp and marked which shelf went quiet last.
journal.3 [16e205] = 你提着旧灯走了一趟夜间静巡，记下了哪个书架最后安静下来。
# en: You followed the wandering section on a string for six hours.
journal.4 [c09fce] = 你牵着一根线，跟着游走的书区走了六个小时。
# en: The first night the shelves moved, the book stayed lost.
journal.5 [200a60] = 书架移动的第一个夜里，那本书还是没找到。
# en: You found the book, eleven years overdue. Every book falls open at the right page for you now.
journal.6 [ecf968] = 你找到了那本逾期十一年的书。如今每本书都会为你翻到正确的那一页。

@event library_footnote_drawer
# en: Footnote's Drawer
title [a6341c] = 脚注的抽屉
# en: Footnote has sat on one catalogue drawer for a week and hisses at anyone who comes near it. The label underneath him says OVERDUE, ELEVEN YEARS. The head librarian says whoever finds that book is welcome to the trick of finding books.
text [426aad] = 脚注已经在一个目录抽屉上蹲了一周，谁靠近就冲谁哈气。它身下的标签写着：逾期，十一年。总馆员说，谁找到那本书，找书的诀窍就归谁。
# en: A long library catalogue cabinet, a large cat sitting immovably on one drawer, a student crouching to read its label.
scene [13482f] = 一排长长的图书馆目录柜，一只大猫纹丝不动地蹲在其中一个抽屉上，一个学生蹲下来读抽屉的标签。
# en: Find out what he's guarding
opt.left.label [f87004] = 看看它守着什么
# en: You read the card around his tail. A book on wards, borrowed by a Professor Thorne, eleven years ago. Footnote looks at you as if you've finally asked the right question.
opt.left.say.1 [0745bd] = 你读了它尾巴周围的卡片。一本关于护界的书，十一年前被一位索恩教授借走。脚注看着你，好像你终于问对了问题。
# en: Shelve around him
opt.right.label [cb3631] = 绕开它上架
# en: You shelve around Footnote for the rest of the shift. He watches every book you put away, as if marking them.
opt.right.say.1 [706e72] = 这一整班你都绕着脚注上架。它盯着你放回的每一本书，好像在打分。

@event library_fish_footnote
# en: Bribing the Cat
title [e6afcd] = 贿赂猫
# en: Footnote won't move from the drawer for less than fish. Good fish, from the village, not the refectory's. The head librarian says this is "between you and the cat".
text [0b74f5] = 不给鱼，脚注就不挪窝。要好鱼，村里的，不是膳堂的。总馆员说这是“你和猫之间的事”。
# en: A student offering a small paper parcel of fish to a large, unimpressed cat on a library cabinet.
scene [f6e2c8] = 一个学生向一只大猫递上一小包纸裹的鱼，猫蹲在图书馆的柜子上，毫不动容。
# en: Buy him a proper herring
opt.left.label [3982c9] = 给它买条好鲱鱼
# en: Footnote eats the herring slowly, looking at you the whole time, then steps off the drawer and onto your lap. The card is yours. So, apparently, is the cat.
opt.left.say.1 [22fcf2] = 脚注慢慢吃着鲱鱼，全程盯着你，然后走下抽屉，走到你腿上。卡片是你的了。看样子，猫也是。
# en: Wait him out
opt.right.label [d67522] = 跟它耗
# en: You wait. Footnote waits better. At closing he yawns, stretches, and lies back down on the drawer.
opt.right.say.1 [e00cf3] = 你等。脚注更会等。闭馆时它打了个哈欠，伸了个懒腰，又在抽屉上躺下了。

@event library_hush_lamp
# en: The Night Hush
title [d45a3e] = 夜间静巡
# en: The overdue book will only be on the shelves the night hush sends it to. The head librarian lends you the old lamp. "Walk the hush," she says, "and listen to which shelf goes quiet last."
text [5a1796] = 那本逾期的书，只会出现在夜间静巡把它送去的书架上。总馆员把那盏旧灯借给你。“去巡一趟静，”她说，“听听哪个书架最后安静下来。”
# en: A dark library reading room at night, a student walking the shelves with a lamp held high while the books seem to lean toward the light.
scene [5702f8] = 夜里黑暗的图书馆阅览室，一个学生高举着灯走过书架，书似乎都朝光倾过来。
# en: Walk the hush and listen
opt.left.label [963e2f] = 巡一趟静，仔细听
# en: Three laps, and on the third, the shelves on the north side go quiet a heartbeat after the rest. You mark it on your map. The lamp seems pleased with you.
opt.left.say.1 [0b4ada] = 走了三圈，第三圈时，北边的书架比其他的晚一拍才安静下来。你在地图上做了标记。那盏灯似乎对你很满意。
# en: Every shelf goes quiet at once, which is either very helpful or a joke at your expense. You walk until midnight and mark nothing.
opt.left.say.2 [8540fc] = 所有书架同时安静下来，这要么非常有用，要么是在拿你开玩笑。你一直巡到午夜，什么也没标出来。
# en: Ask the head librarian outright
opt.right.label [dab481] = 直接问总馆员
# en: "If I told you," she says, "you wouldn't have found it." She gives you extra shelving for asking.
opt.right.say.1 [47780a] = “要是我告诉你，”她说，“你就不会找到了。”她因为你问了这句，给你多派了些上架的活。

@event library_wandering_section
# en: The Wandering Section
title [ed4770] = 游走的书区
# en: The section the book belongs to wanders. It was by the stairs on Monday and in the map room on Wednesday. The only way to follow it is to tie a string to the end shelf and walk where it goes, however long that takes.
text [7df408] = 那本书所在的书区会游走。周一它在楼梯边，周三在地图室。想跟上它，只能把一根线拴在末端书架上，它去哪儿你跟到哪儿，不管要多久。
# en: A student trailing a long ball of string through a maze of library shelves that have visibly rearranged themselves behind them.
scene [4023b6] = 一个学生拖着一长团线穿行在图书馆的书架迷宫里，身后的书架明显已经重新排列过了。
# en: Follow it with string
opt.left.label [66d2f0] = 拴根线跟着它
# en: You follow it for six hours, through rooms you didn't know the library had. At the end you know its route by heart and never want to see a ball of string again.
opt.left.say.1 [fd7610] = 你跟了它六个小时，穿过一些你不知道图书馆有的房间。最后你把它的路线背得滚瓜烂熟，再也不想看见线团了。
# en: Wait for it to come back
opt.right.label [4c2d5a] = 等它自己回来
# en: You read at the desk until the section wanders past again, a day later. You learn nothing about its route, and a little about medieval ward-lattices.
opt.right.say.1 [6bbd90] = 你在桌边看书，等那个书区一天后又游过来。你没弄清它的路线，倒是对中世纪的护界晶格懂了一点。

@event library_overdue_book
# en: Eleven Years Overdue
title [8b1cf2] = 逾期十一年
# en: Tonight the shelves are moving. Somewhere in the wandering section is the book, eleven years overdue, and every book you touch tries to fall open at the wrong page. {flag(index_fish): Footnote is on your shoulder.|You're on your own.}
text [b8e5d2] = 今晚书架在移动。那本逾期十一年的书就在游走的书区某处，你碰到的每一本书都想翻到错的那一页。{flag(index_fish): 脚注蹲在你肩上。|你只能靠自己。}
# en: A student high on a rolling ladder in a library where the shelves are visibly moving, a cat on their shoulder, one dusty book glowing faintly.
scene [1570eb] = 一个学生站在移动梯的高处，图书馆的书架明显在移动，一只猫蹲在学生肩上，一本落满灰的书发着微光。
# en: Find the page
opt.left.label [672d94] = 找到那一页
# en: Your hand finds the spine before your eyes do, and the book falls open at exactly the page it was borrowed for. Every book you touch afterwards does the same. The head librarian stamps the card, eleven years late, without a word.
opt.left.say.1 [0c241a] = 你的手比眼睛先摸到书脊，书正好翻开在当年被借走的那一页。此后你碰到的每本书都这样。总馆员一言不发地在卡片上盖了章，晚了十一年。
# en: You get lost on the seventh floor among shelves that don't exist by day. Footnote leads you out at dawn, looking smug. The card is still on the drawer.
opt.left.say.2 [e48270] = 你在一些白天并不存在的书架之间迷失在七楼。天亮时脚注一脸得意地把你领了出来。卡片还在抽屉上。
# en: Pay a senior clerk for their map
opt.right.label [cbd312] = 花钱买资深职员的地图
# en: The senior clerk's map is ten years out of date and exactly right where it matters. You find the book, and it falls open at the page it was borrowed for. Every book does, after that.
opt.right.say.1 [c585bc] = 资深职员的地图过时了十年，但在要紧的地方分毫不差。你找到了那本书，它翻开在被借走的那一页。从那以后，每本书都这样。
# en: The map is ten years out of date and mostly wrong. Footnote leads you out at dawn. The book stays lost, for now.
opt.right.say.2 [d1b216] = 地图过时了十年，大部分是错的。天亮时脚注把你领了出来。那本书暂时还丢着。

@thread rapport_quest
# en: Two taps on the bar
name [12c408] = 吧台上敲两下
# en: The Newt's landlady stops fights with two taps and one sentence.
premise [9210b7] = 蝾螈酒馆的老板娘敲两下吧台、说一句话，就能把一场架拦下来。
# en: "Can't teach it," the landlady said. "You earn it. Learn the room, buy the room, work the room."
journal.1 [1909d4] = “这教不了，”老板娘说，“得自己挣来。摸清这屋子，请这屋子喝一轮，镇住这屋子。”
# en: You learned the old barge-man's eel story and told it back.
journal.2 [7b5c40] = 你学会了老驳船工的鳗鱼故事，又讲给大家听。
# en: You stood the regulars' corner a round. They know your name now.
journal.3 [840029] = 你请熟客角喝了一轮。现在他们都知道你的名字了。
# en: Fourteen hours on your feet: now you can read the room from across it.
journal.4 [f0d193] = 站了十四个小时：现在你隔着整间屋子就能看懂里面的人。
# en: The first night the room was yours, it got away from you.
journal.5 [8b2bf1] = 第一次让你独自看场的那夜，场子没镇住。
# en: You held the Newt on a packed night. The landlady knew at once, and nodded.
journal.6 [9a40b0] = 一个满座的夜里，你镇住了蝾螈酒馆。老板娘一回来就知道了，点了点头。

@event tavern_two_taps
# en: Two Taps on the Bar
title [6ad648] = 吧台上敲两下
# en: Two barge-men are halfway out of their chairs when the landlady taps the bar twice, says one sentence you don't catch, and the whole room laughs instead. The fight is over before it began. She catches you staring. "Want to know how?"
text [5be858] = 两个驳船工半个身子已经离了椅子，老板娘在吧台上敲了两下，说了一句你没听清的话，整个酒馆就笑了起来。架还没打就散了。她发现你在盯着看。“想知道怎么做到的吗？”
# en: A crowded tavern on the edge of a brawl, a landlady tapping the bar twice and the whole room suddenly laughing instead.
scene [0feadf] = 一家拥挤的酒馆眼看要打起来，老板娘在吧台上敲了两下，满屋子的人忽然都笑了。
# en: "Yes. Teach me."
opt.left.label [8d2667] = “想。教我。”
# en: "Can't teach it," she says. "You earn it. Learn the room, buy the room, work the room." She taps the bar twice at you, and you laugh, and you don't know why.
opt.left.say.1 [f853d9] = “教不了，”她说，“得自己挣。了解这间屋子，请这间屋子喝一轮，在这间屋子里干活。”她冲你在吧台上敲了两下，你笑了，却不知道为什么。
# en: Keep pouring
opt.right.label [d1291a] = 接着倒酒
# en: You keep pouring. The barge-men buy each other a drink and sing. The landlady watches you, thoughtfully, for the rest of the shift.
opt.right.say.1 [39eec5] = 你接着倒酒。驳船工们互相请了一杯，唱起歌来。这一班剩下的时间，老板娘若有所思地看着你。

@event tavern_eel_story
# en: The Eel Story
title [77827b] = 鳗鱼的故事
# en: The old barge-man's eel story is the most famous story at the Newt. Regulars mouth along. The landlady says if you can tell it as well as he does, the room will be half yours. He's willing to teach it, slowly, for an evening.
text [891f3d] = 老驳船工的鳗鱼故事是蝾螈酒馆最有名的故事。熟客们会跟着念。老板娘说，你要是能讲得和他一样好，这屋子就有一半归你。他愿意花一个晚上，慢慢教你。
# en: A barge-man at a tavern table with his arms spread wide, telling a story to a student taking notes on a bar napkin.
scene [0b5a36] = 酒馆桌边一位老驳船工张开双臂讲故事，一个学生在吧台的餐巾上记笔记。
# en: Learn it and tell it back
opt.left.label [25ce86] = 学会它，讲回去
# en: You tell it back that same night, to the same corner, and get the laugh at the eel's second escape. The barge-man wipes his eyes and buys you a cider.
opt.left.say.1 [692985] = 当晚你就对着同一个角落讲了回去，在鳗鱼第二次逃跑时赢得了笑声。老驳船工抹着眼泪，请你喝了一杯苹果酒。
# en: You get the eel's name wrong and the ending backwards. The regulars are very kind about it, which is worse.
opt.left.say.2 [f8158d] = 你把鳗鱼的名字讲错了，结尾也讲反了。熟客们对此非常体贴，这反而更糟。
# en: Just enjoy the story
opt.right.label [0efa4a] = 就好好听故事
# en: You sit and listen to the eel story twice through, and laugh both times. You couldn't tell it, but you've rarely had a better evening.
opt.right.say.1 [03bb5d] = 你坐下来把鳗鱼的故事从头听了两遍，两遍都笑了。你讲不出来，但你很少有过比这更好的晚上。

@event tavern_regulars_round
# en: The Regulars' Corner
title [98ab7f] = 熟客角
# en: The regulars' corner has never had a round bought by staff. The landlady says that's exactly why you should. "Nobody listens to a story from someone who's never stood them a drink."
text [cecaa4] = 熟客角从没被店员请过一轮。老板娘说这正是你该请的理由。“没请人喝过一杯的人讲的故事，没人会听。”
# en: A student setting down a tray of mugs at a crowded corner table in a tavern, the regulars raising them in a toast.
scene [c4c30c] = 一个学生把一托盘杯子放在酒馆拥挤的角落桌上，熟客们举杯敬酒。
# en: Stand the corner a round
opt.left.label [e38d06] = 请熟客角喝一轮
# en: The corner raises the mugs to you, by name, which you didn't know they knew. For the rest of the night they call you over to settle every argument.
opt.left.say.1 [96836a] = 熟客角举杯敬你，叫出了你的名字，你都不知道他们知道你叫什么。那一晚剩下的时间，每有争执他们都叫你过去评理。
# en: Keep your tips
opt.right.label [224ca7] = 留着你的小费
# en: You pocket your tips. The corner doesn't notice either way, which is rather the point.
opt.right.say.1 [2ed62f] = 你把小费揣进兜里。熟客角对此毫无察觉，这恰恰就是重点。

@event tavern_double_shift
# en: The Double Shift
title [6df679] = 双班
# en: Two servers are down with Lake Fever, and the landlady needs a double shift: lunch through closing. "You'll learn more about a room in fourteen hours," she says, "than in a term of evenings."
text [d66301] = 两个侍应得了湖热病，老板娘需要一个人上双班：从午饭一直到打烊。“十四个钟头，”她说，“你对一间屋子的了解，会比一学期的晚班还多。”
# en: A tired student wiping down a bar at closing time after a very long day, the landlady counting the till beside them.
scene [6435ce] = 打烊时分，一个疲惫的学生在擦吧台，干了很长的一天，老板娘在旁边数钱柜。
# en: Work the double
opt.left.label [63ca5c] = 上这个双班
# en: Fourteen hours on your feet. By closing you can tell who wants to talk and who wants to be left alone from across the room. Your feet are a separate, angrier person.
opt.left.say.1 [334ef3] = 站了十四个钟头。打烊时，你隔着整间屋子就能看出谁想聊天、谁想清静。你的脚已经成了另一个更暴躁的人。
# en: Turn it down
opt.right.label [99bc49] = 推掉
# en: You say you can't. The landlady works it herself, and is short with you for a week.
opt.right.say.1 [e083d3] = 你说你干不了。老板娘自己顶上了，一周都对你没好脸色。

@event tavern_festival_room
# en: The Room Is Yours
title [05ee85] = 这间屋子归你了
# en: The landlady is away for the night and the Newt is packed to the rafters, two barges in and a fight brewing by the fire. It's yours to hold. {flag(rapport_eel) and flag(rapport_round) and flag(rapport_shift): You know this room now.|You know some of this room.}
text [2f03ff] = 老板娘今晚不在，蝾螈酒馆挤得满满当当，来了两条驳船的人，壁炉边还有一场架在酝酿。这间屋子归你镇住。{flag(rapport_eel) and flag(rapport_round) and flag(rapport_shift): 你现在了解这间屋子。|这间屋子你只了解一部分。}
# en: A packed tavern on a festival night, a student standing on a chair telling a story while the crowd hangs on every word.
scene [da8c84] = 节日夜挤得满满的酒馆，一个学生站在椅子上讲故事，人群屏息听着每一个字。
# en: Tap the bar twice
opt.left.label [ef6f14] = 在吧台上敲两下
# en: You tap the bar twice, say one sentence about an eel, and the room laughs. The fight by the fire turns into a song. When the landlady comes back, she knows at once. She just nods.
opt.left.say.1 [a874d5] = 你在吧台上敲了两下，说了一句关于鳗鱼的话，满屋子都笑了。壁炉边的那场架变成了一首歌。老板娘回来时一眼就明白了。她只是点点头。
# en: The tap comes out as a knock and the laugh never comes. A chair breaks, and so do some glasses, and the fine comes out of your wages. Next festival night, she says, you can try again.
opt.left.say.2 [b92402] = 敲出来成了叩门声，笑声始终没来。一把椅子断了，几只杯子碎了，罚款从你的工钱里扣。下一个节日夜，她说，你可以再试。
# en: Buy the first round, then talk
opt.right.label [8de009] = 先请一轮，再开口
# en: A round on the house first, then a story while they drink it. By the time the mugs are empty, nobody remembers wanting to fight. The landlady hears about it before she's through the door.
opt.right.say.1 [1ac8d6] = 先请全场喝一轮，趁他们喝的时候讲个故事。等杯子见了底，谁也不记得自己想打架了。老板娘还没进门就听说了。
# en: They drink the round and fight anyway. You mop up with the rest of the staff. Next festival night, the landlady says.
opt.right.say.2 [ca000a] = 他们喝了那一轮，照样打了起来。你和其他店员一起收拾残局。下一个节日夜，老板娘说。

@thread distil_quest
# en: Pell's oldest drawer
name [16c158] = 佩尔最老的抽屉
# en: A yellowed card in Pell's oldest drawer: a draught "of your own strength".
premise [c0d0e8] = 佩尔最老的抽屉里有一张发黄的卡片：一剂“取自己之力”的药。
# en: You copied out the old draught's recipe. Pell corrected one of your measures, which is permission.
journal.1 [849870] = 你抄下了那剂老药的方子。佩尔替你改了一个剂量，这就算是准许了。
# en: You counted four hundred and twelve drops with Pell and didn't lose count. "Fair," he said.
journal.2 [0f0ad2] = 你陪佩尔数了四百一十二滴，一次也没数错。“还行，”他说。
# en: You bought the good moonwort and carried it home without humming.
journal.3 [aca8b4] = 你买下了上好的月蕨，一路没哼歌地把它带回了家。
# en: You tasted the draught first, the daughters' way, and spent a day in bed learning where it pulls from.
journal.4 [970669] = 你照女儿们的法子先尝了一口，在床上躺了一天，弄清了它从哪里抽走力气。
# en: The first brew boiled over and took more out of you than it should.
journal.5 [38da21] = 第一次熬药时锅沸溢了，从你身上抽走的比该抽的还多。
# en: The draught came down to one shining drop. Pell stopped counting. "Fair."
journal.6 [dfc6ac] = 那剂药凝成了闪亮的一滴。佩尔停下了数数。“还行。”

@event pell_oldest_drawer
# en: The Oldest Drawer
title [6f192c] = 最老的抽屉
# en: Restocking, you open the oldest drawer at the bottom of Pell's wall. Inside is one yellowed card: a draught "of your own strength", in a hand older than Pell's. Pell sees it and counts to three under his breath. "That one costs the brewer," he says. "Measure twice."
text [24f57e] = 补货时，你打开了佩尔那面墙最底下最老的抽屉。里面只有一张泛黄的卡片：一剂“取自本身之力”的药，笔迹比佩尔的还老。佩尔看见了，低声数到三。“那剂药要熬药的人付出代价，”他说，“量两遍。”
# en: An old apothecary's wall of tiny drawers, one at the very bottom pulled open to reveal a yellowed recipe card, a gruff old man watching from the counter.
scene [186551] = 一面老药铺的小抽屉墙，最底下的一个被拉开，露出一张泛黄的配方卡，一个粗声粗气的老人在柜台边看着。
# en: Copy the recipe
opt.left.label [077927] = 抄下配方
# en: You copy it out carefully. Pell watches you do it and says nothing, then corrects one of your measures in your copy. That is the closest he comes to permission.
opt.left.say.1 [3d8ed7] = 你仔仔细细地抄了一份。佩尔看着你抄，什么也没说，然后改正了你抄本里的一个剂量。这已经是他最接近“准许”的表示了。
# en: Close the drawer
opt.right.label [f59ddd] = 关上抽屉
# en: You close it. Pell nods once and goes back to his scales. Later you notice he has relabelled the drawer, clearly, "Not yet."
opt.right.say.1 [6b9f22] = 你把它关上了。佩尔点了一下头，回去看他的秤。后来你发现他把抽屉的标签换了，写得清清楚楚：“还没到时候。”

@event pell_counting_drops
# en: Counting Drops
title [77984e] = 数药滴
# en: Pell distills by the drop, all night, counting aloud. "If you mean to try the old draught," he says, "you'll count with me first. Lose count once and we start again."
text [be6174] = 佩尔蒸馏是一滴一滴来的，整夜大声数着。“你要是想试那剂老药，”他说，“就先陪我数一夜。数错一次就从头来。”
# en: A dim apothecary at night, an old man and a student bent over a slowly dripping still, both counting under their breath.
scene [762f29] = 夜里昏暗的药铺，一个老人和一个学生俯身在一台缓缓滴落的蒸馏器前，两人都在低声数数。
# en: Count all night with him
opt.left.label [5b4fd1] = 陪他数一整夜
# en: Four hundred and twelve drops, and you don't lose count once. At dawn Pell says "Fair," which is once a decade, and lets you stopper the bottle.
opt.left.say.1 [f234d7] = 四百一十二滴，你一次都没数错。天亮时佩尔说了声“公道”，十年才说一次，并让你给瓶子塞上了塞。
# en: You lose count at three hundred and something. Pell starts again without comment. So do you. You lose it again.
opt.left.say.2 [504e92] = 数到三百多时你数乱了。佩尔一言不发地从头开始。你也是。你又数乱了。
# en: Go home and sleep
opt.right.label [9aa5d0] = 回家睡觉
# en: You go home. Pell counts on alone, steadily, through the night. In the morning the bottle is full and labelled, and he says nothing about it.
opt.right.say.1 [45817c] = 你回家了。佩尔一个人稳稳地数了一整夜。早上瓶子满了，贴好了标签，他对此只字未提。

@event pell_buy_moonwort
# en: Moonwort
title [66d660] = 月蕨
# en: The old draught needs moonwort, and the only good moonwort in the village is the jar on Pell's top shelf, labelled "Do not hum near." Pell sells it to staff at cost. The cost is not small.
text [3ca560] = 那剂老药需要月蕨，而村里唯一好的月蕨就在佩尔最高那层架子上的罐子里，标签写着“附近勿哼歌”。佩尔按成本价卖给店员。成本可不低。
# en: An apothecary counter with a small jar labelled "Moonwort. Do not hum near.", a student counting out coins beside it.
scene [18cf79] = 药铺柜台上一个标着“月蕨，附近勿哼歌”的小罐子，一个学生在旁边数着硬币。
# en: Buy the moonwort
opt.left.label [d9f851] = 买下月蕨
# en: Pell weighs it twice and wraps it in waxed paper. You carry it home without humming, which is harder than it sounds.
opt.left.say.1 [3e1ea5] = 佩尔称了两遍，用蜡纸包好。你一路没哼歌把它带回了家，这比听起来难。
# en: Try the cheap substitute
opt.right.label [162b22] = 试试便宜的替代品
# en: The substitute smells wrong the moment you open it. Pell takes it from you without a word and puts it in the bin.
opt.right.say.1 [15c4d9] = 替代品一打开就不对味。佩尔一言不发地从你手里拿走，扔进了垃圾桶。

@event pell_daughters_shortcut
# en: The Daughters' Shortcut
title [ac5208] = 女儿们的捷径
# en: Pell's daughters say there's a shortcut: learn what the draught takes out of a brewer by tasting a little of it first. "Father hates it," says one. "It works," says the other. "You'll be ill for a day."
text [4ba2b2] = 佩尔的女儿们说有条捷径：先尝一点，弄清这剂药会从熬药人身上拿走什么。“父亲讨厌这个，”一个说。“但管用，”另一个说，“你会病一天。”
# en: The back room of an apothecary, a student drinking a small cup of something dark while two women watch with professional interest.
scene [33c062] = 药铺的里屋，一个学生喝下一小杯深色的东西，两个女人带着职业性的兴趣看着。
# en: Try it on yourself
opt.left.label [164155] = 在自己身上试
# en: It takes the strength out of your knees and then, slowly, gives it back. You spend a day in bed. When you get up, you know exactly where the draught will pull from.
opt.left.say.1 [39fb0c] = 它先把力气从你膝盖里抽走，再慢慢还回来。你在床上躺了一天。起来时，你清楚地知道这剂药会从哪里抽力。
# en: Do it Pell's way
opt.right.label [7b2559] = 按佩尔的规矩来
# en: You decline. The daughters shrug. Pell, who was listening, corrects a label more firmly than it needed.
opt.right.say.1 [fb421f] = 你谢绝了。女儿们耸耸肩。一直在听的佩尔，把一张标签改得比需要的更用力。

@event pell_draught
# en: Of Your Own Strength
title [96c35c] = 取自本身之力
# en: Pell closes the shop early, sets the old still on the bench and holds the lamp himself. "Brew it," he says. "I'll count." The recipe card lies beside you. {flag(distil_drops) and flag(distil_moonwort) and flag(distil_shortcut): You know every step of it.|There are steps you haven't practised.}
text [1dc449] = 佩尔提早关了店，把那台老蒸馏器放在工作台上，亲自掌灯。“熬吧，”他说，“我来数。”配方卡就放在你手边。{flag(distil_drops) and flag(distil_moonwort) and flag(distil_shortcut): 每一步你都了然于心。|有几步你还没练过。}
# en: An apothecary's still at night, a student drawing a single shining drop out of a dark mixture while an old man holds the lamp.
scene [ebd457] = 夜里药铺的蒸馏器旁，一个学生从深色混合物中萃出一滴闪亮的液体，一个老人举着灯。
# en: Brew the draught
opt.left.label [b27087] = 熬这剂药
# en: The draught comes down to one shining drop, and as it falls you feel exactly what it took from you, and how to take it again. Pell stops counting. "Fair," he says, twice in one year.
opt.left.say.1 [50ca10] = 那剂药浓缩成闪亮的一滴，落下时你清楚地感觉到它从你身上拿走了什么，以及怎样再拿一次。佩尔停止了数数。“公道，”他说，一年里说了两次。
# en: The mixture boils over and takes more out of you than it should. Pell puts the card back in the drawer and writes "Don't." on the front. Next term, perhaps.
opt.left.say.2 [fbced8] = 混合物沸溢了，从你身上拿走的比该拿的多。佩尔把卡片放回抽屉，在正面写上“别”。也许下学期吧。
# en: Use Pell's own moonwort stock
opt.right.label [f7c024] = 用佩尔自己的月蕨存货
# en: With the good stock, it comes down clean to one drop. You feel it pull, and you feel where it pulls from. Pell writes the cost in his ledger, and your name beside the recipe.
opt.right.say.1 [43bab8] = 用了好存货，它干干净净地浓缩成一滴。你感觉到它在拉扯，也感觉到它从哪儿拉扯。佩尔把成本记进账本，在配方旁写上了你的名字。
# en: Even with his best stock it boils over. Pell writes "Don't." on the drawer and the cost in the ledger. Next term, perhaps.
opt.right.say.2 [2fc843] = 就算用了他最好的存货，它还是沸溢了。佩尔在抽屉上写了“别”，把成本记进了账本。也许下学期吧。

@thread tailwind_quest
# en: The jar of wind
name [4a78a8] = 罐中之风
# en: A stoppered jar on the dead-letter shelf: FOR WHOEVER IS FAST ENOUGH.
premise [5304e7] = 死信架上一只塞着瓶塞的罐子：给够快的人。
# en: You took the wind jar down. The loft master wrote your name under one too faded to read.
journal.1 [6f23b3] = 你把那罐风取了下来。阁楼主管在一个褪色到看不清的名字下面写上了你的名字。
# en: The old fisherman flew the jar once. Never stop, he said. Stopping's what kills it.
journal.2 [67182d] = 老渔夫曾带着这只罐子飞过。别停下，他说。一停，风就死了。
# en: You beat the gulls from the jetty to the far bank, and the wind in the jar turned over once.
journal.3 [bfb8be] = 你从码头到对岸赢过了海鸥，罐子里的风翻了个身。
# en: You had your broom trued. It flies straight for the first time in living memory.
journal.4 [b033c5] = 你把扫帚找人校直了。有人记得以来，它头一回飞得笔直。
# en: The first storm run, a gust took you into the shallows.
journal.5 [878b0c] = 第一次冒着风暴送件时，一阵狂风把你吹进了浅滩。
# en: You crossed the lake in a storm with the wind behind you. It stays when you call it.
journal.6 [83e9e9] = 你在风暴中带着身后的风飞过了湖。如今你一唤，它就留下。

@event courier_wind_jar
# en: Wind in a Jar
title [396974] = 罐中之风
# en: On the dead-letter shelf, behind a parcel addressed to nobody, is a stoppered jar with a wind in it, going round and round. The label says FOR WHOEVER IS FAST ENOUGH. The loft master says someone flew with it once, before her time.
text [ccddb6] = 在死信架上，一个寄给“无人”的包裹后面，有一只塞着瓶塞的罐子，里面有一阵风在打转。标签上写着：给够快的人。阁楼主管说，在她之前有人带着它飞过。
# en: A courier loft with a dusty shelf of unclaimed letters, a student holding up a stoppered jar in which a small wind is visibly whirling.
scene [973bd6] = 一间信使阁楼，落满灰的架子上摆着无人认领的信，一个学生举起一只塞着瓶塞的罐子，里面一小阵风明显在打转。
# en: Take the jar down
opt.left.label [b3ece8] = 把罐子取下来
# en: The jar hums in your hands, and every broom in the loft leans toward you. The loft master writes your name on the jar's label, under a name too faded to read.
opt.left.say.1 [8ae601] = 罐子在你手里嗡嗡作响，阁楼里每一把扫帚都朝你倾过来。阁楼主管把你的名字写在罐子的标签上，就在一个褪色得认不出的名字下面。
# en: Leave it on the shelf
opt.right.label [52ecc9] = 留在架子上
# en: You leave it for whoever is fast enough. You fly your round. The jar's wind stirs the dead letters as you go.
opt.right.say.1 [967b48] = 你把它留给够快的人。你飞你的线路。你走时，罐中之风吹动了那些死信。

@event courier_fisherman_waves
# en: The Fisherman Waves
title [c74709] = 渔夫挥手了
# en: The old fisherman in the reed beds has never waved at a courier. Today, seeing the jar strapped to your broom, he waves, and beckons you down. "That jar," he says. "I flew it once. Fastest year of my life."
text [9be0ca] = 芦苇丛里那个老渔夫从来不向信使挥手。今天他看见绑在你扫帚上的罐子，挥了挥手，招呼你下来。“那个罐子，”他说，“我带它飞过。那是我这辈子最快的一年。”
# en: An old fisherman in a small boat on a grey lake waving up at a student on a broom flying low overhead.
scene [8d25dd] = 灰色湖面上一条小船里，一个老渔夫朝低空飞过的骑扫帚学生挥手。
# en: Land and ask him about it
opt.left.label [6354d0] = 落下来问他
# en: He tells you, slowly, between casts: you don't fly the wind, you let it get behind you and keep going. Never stop. "Stopping's what kills it," he says, and goes back to his line.
opt.left.say.1 [cedb6e] = 他在两次甩竿之间慢慢告诉你：风不是你驾驭的，你让它绕到身后，然后一直往前。永不停下。“停下才会害死它，”他说完，又回去守他的鱼线。
# en: He talks about fish for an hour, then says the light's going, and rows off. You'll have to come back.
opt.left.say.2 [6f6d6d] = 他讲了一个钟头的鱼，然后说天色晚了，划走了。你只能改天再来。
# en: Wave back and fly on
opt.right.label [0c1d4c] = 挥手回应，继续飞
# en: You wave and fly on with your round, on time. He watches you go, and doesn't wave again.
opt.right.say.1 [fcc4c8] = 你挥了挥手，继续飞你的线路，准时送达。他看着你离开，没再挥手。

@event courier_race_gulls
# en: Racing the Gulls
title [9ce849] = 和海鸥比赛
# en: The gulls over the lake race couriers for fun. The fisherman says the jar's wind won't follow you until you've beaten them once, flat out, from the jetty to the far bank.
text [88930f] = 湖上的海鸥喜欢和信使比赛取乐。渔夫说，除非你全速从码头飞到对岸、赢它们一次，否则罐中之风不会跟随你。
# en: A student on a broom flying flat out over a lake in a cloud of wheeling gulls, letters fluttering in a satchel.
scene [ea7b1f] = 一个学生骑着扫帚在一群盘旋的海鸥中全速飞过湖面，挎包里的信在扑扑作响。
# en: Race them flat out
opt.left.label [2cf84d] = 全速和它们比
# en: You hit the far bank a beak ahead of the lead gull. The wind in the jar turns over once, like a cat settling. The gulls follow you home, offended.
opt.left.say.1 [137ff7] = 你比领头的海鸥早一个鸟嘴到达对岸。罐子里的风翻了个身，像一只猫安顿下来。海鸥们跟着你回家，很是不服。
# en: You clip a wave at full speed and skip across the lake like a stone. The gulls are delighted. You are wet to the bone.
opt.left.say.2 [c26046] = 你全速擦到一个浪头，像打水漂的石子一样在湖面上蹦了出去。海鸥们乐坏了。你湿透到了骨头。
# en: Fly your round steady
opt.right.label [e3e15d] = 稳稳飞你的线路
# en: You fly the round steady and deliver everything dry. The gulls lose interest. So does the jar.
opt.right.say.1 [efd0ae] = 你稳稳飞完线路，所有东西都送得干干的。海鸥们没了兴趣。罐子也是。

@event courier_fix_broom
# en: The Broom That Pulls Left
title [146da3] = 总往左偏的扫帚
# en: Your loft broom pulls left, always has. With the jar's wind behind it, it would pull you into the lake. The broom-maker in the village can true it, for a price.
text [c55b82] = 你那把阁楼扫帚总往左偏，一直如此。要是罐中之风在后面推，它会把你直接拽进湖里。村里的扫帚匠能把它调直，要价不菲。
# en: A broom-maker's bench in the village, a craftsman sighting along a broom handle while a student waits with their satchel.
scene [e4d60b] = 村里扫帚匠的工作台，一位工匠顺着扫帚柄瞄看，一个学生背着挎包在旁边等。
# en: Pay to have it trued
opt.left.label [060449] = 付钱把它调直
# en: The broom-maker sights along it, tuts, and spends an afternoon on it. It flies straight for the first time in living memory. You miss the pull, a little.
opt.left.say.1 [d2dfad] = 扫帚匠顺着柄瞄了瞄，啧了一声，花了一下午调它。它飞得笔直，有史以来头一回。你倒有点怀念那股偏劲了。
# en: Learn to fly it crooked
opt.right.label [dc7c45] = 学会歪着飞
# en: You learn to lean right all the time. Your back complains, and the broom keeps pulling left out of habit.
opt.right.say.1 [a75c5e] = 你学会了一直往右倾。你的背在抗议，扫帚出于习惯还是往左偏。

@event courier_storm_delivery
# en: The Storm Run
title [a96ce0] = 风暴快递
# en: A storm is down on the lake, and a parcel must cross it tonight. The loft master looks at the jar at your belt, then at you. "Nobody else will go," she says. {flag(tailwind_fisherman) and flag(tailwind_gulls) and flag(tailwind_broom): You know how to let the wind get behind you.|You've never flown it in weather.}
text [272501] = 湖上压着一场风暴，一个包裹今晚必须送过去。阁楼主管看看你腰间的罐子，又看看你。“没别人肯去，”她说。{flag(tailwind_fisherman) and flag(tailwind_gulls) and flag(tailwind_broom): 你知道怎么让风绕到身后。|你从没在恶劣天气里飞过它。}
# en: A student on a broom flying through a storm over a dark lake, a jar of wind unstoppered at their belt, lightning behind them.
scene [5e21d4] = 一个学生骑着扫帚在黑暗的湖上穿过风暴，腰间一只拔开塞子的罐子里装着风，身后电光闪闪。
# en: Open the jar and go
opt.left.label [f5ca84] = 打开罐子，出发
# en: You pull the stopper and the wind gets behind you and doesn't stop. You cross the lake faster than the lightning can find you. The parcel arrives dry. The wind stays with you after, when you call it.
opt.left.say.1 [04a55b] = 你拔开瓶塞，风绕到你身后，再也没停。你穿过湖面，快得闪电都找不到你。包裹送到时还是干的。从那以后，你一唤，风就跟着你。
# en: Halfway across, a gust takes you and you ditch in the shallows. The parcel survives. You barely do. The next storm season, the loft master says, you can try again.
opt.left.say.2 [17bc2c] = 飞到一半，一阵狂风把你掀了下去，你栽进了浅滩。包裹保住了。你差点没保住。下一个风暴季，阁楼主管说，你可以再试。
# en: Wait for the lull, then go
opt.right.label [6f2d3e] = 等风势稍缓再出发
# en: You wait, nerves screaming, for the gap in the storm, then open the jar and go. The wind gets behind you and stays. The parcel arrives an hour late and dry, and the wind is yours.
opt.right.say.1 [267a25] = 你等着，神经绷得快要尖叫，等风暴露出那道缝，然后打开罐子出发。风绕到你身后，一直没走。包裹晚到了一个钟头，干干的，那阵风归你了。
# en: The lull never comes, and you go anyway and ditch in the shallows. The next storm season, the loft master says.
opt.right.say.2 [1cbca9] = 风势始终没缓，你还是出发了，栽进了浅滩。下一个风暴季，阁楼主管说。
